<phrase>
  id: LANG_BLACKJACK_HELP_AIM
  desc: in Blackjack's Help, the first paragraph: the aim and the rules; J, Q and K are the jack, queen and king, written as the cards in your language mark them
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Get closer to 21 than the dealer without going over. Cards count as their number, J, Q and K as 10, and an ace as 1 or 11. The dealer takes cards until reaching 17 or more. A win pays your bet, and a blackjack, 21 with your first two cards, pays 3 to 2."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Lumapit sa 21 nang higit sa dealer nang hindi lumalampas. Ang mga baraha ay katumbas ng kanilang numero, ang J, Q at K ay 10, at ang alas ay 1 o 11. Kumukuha ng baraha ang dealer hanggang umabot sa 17 o higit pa. Ang panalo ay nagbabayad ng iyong taya, at ang blackjack, 21 sa iyong unang dalawang baraha, ay nagbabayad ng 3 sa 2."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_BLACKJACK_HELP_KEYS
  desc: in Blackjack's Help, the second paragraph: the buttons during a hand. Select and Menu are the iPod's buttons, ◀ and ▶ its Previous and Next buttons kept as these signs; Resume Game as that row of the game's menu is translated
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Select takes another card, and ▶ stands. ◀ doubles down on your first two cards: your bet doubles, and you take one more card only. Menu leaves the hand for the menu, and Resume Game goes back to it."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Sa Select, kukuha ka ng isa pang baraha, at sa ▶, titigil ka na. Ang ◀ ay nagda-double down sa iyong unang dalawang baraha: dodoble ang iyong taya, at isa na lang na baraha ang kukunin mo. Iniiwan ng Menu ang kamay para sa menu, at ibinabalik ka rito ng Ituloy ang Laro."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_BLACKJACK_HELP_BET
  desc: in Blackjack's Help, the third paragraph: the bet. ◀ and ▶ are the iPod's Previous and Next buttons kept as these signs, the wheel its click wheel, Select and Menu its buttons; the amounts are dollars
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Before each hand, set your bet: ◀ and ▶ change it by 1, the wheel by 10, and Select deals. Menu ends the game. You start with $1000, and the game is over when less than $10 is left."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Bago ang bawat kamay, itakda ang iyong taya: binabago ito ng ◀ at ▶ nang 1, ng gulong nang 10, at namimigay ng baraha ang Select. Tinatapos ng Menu ang laro. Magsisimula ka sa $1000, at tapos na ang laro kapag mas mababa sa $10 ang natitira."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_BLACKJACK_HELP_QUESTIONS
  desc: in Blackjack's Help, the last paragraph: insurance, splitting and answering the questions the game asks. ◀ and ▶ are the iPod's Previous and Next buttons kept as these signs; Yes and No as the answers are translated
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "When the dealer shows an ace, you can buy insurance for up to half your bet; it pays 2 to 1 if the dealer has blackjack. Two cards of the same rank can be split into two hands, each with your bet. In a question, ◀ and ▶ choose Yes or No, Select answers, and Menu answers No."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Kapag alas ang ipinakita ng dealer, puwede kang bumili ng insurance hanggang kalahati ng iyong taya; nagbabayad ito ng 2 sa 1 kung may blackjack ang dealer. Ang dalawang barahang magkapareho ang ranggo ay puwedeng i-split sa dalawang kamay, bawat isa ay may taya mo. Sa isang tanong, pumipili ang ◀ at ▶ ng Oo o Hindi, sumasagot ang Select, at Hindi ang sagot ng Menu."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
